{
  "name": "bee",
  "_about": "A bee -- the western honeybee (Apis mellifera), a worker 13 mm long: a head and thorax covered in fawn hair, hairy compound eyes and three ocelli on the crown; elbowed antennae; the gaster amber-brown, each ring's back edge black-brown and a band of pale hair at its front; a barbed sting; on each hind leg the broad flat tibia of the pollen basket (the variant \"with pollen\": packed with an orange load); four clear, finely veined wings folded flat over the gaster at rest. Coats: the dark European bee (Apis mellifera mellifera) and the golden Italian. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/hymen.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, elbowed antennae that wave, the wings folded flat over the abdomen -- swung out and beating in the variant \"flying\").",
